    "note": "What each control's cell says where a theme plays this conversation (the bird-labels round, 10-18, his words: \"label more specific to the immediate role of the position\"), in the ring's own table's shape (src/bird-labels.json): `big.reads` is the reading of `conversationLeans` its bands cut and its leans read (`pole` the share of casts a pole's voice takes, -1 every cast the small bells', +1 the great bell's; `count`, `lively`, `leave`, `hard`, `pulse`, `rests` the knobs of `birds`), `big.plan` the tempo where the big word is the plan's, and `big.air` the voice of the record whose air is the big word (Zephyr: the caller's, measured in voice-air.json and cut on the general table's air scale, `{air}` in a line). A cut is never a number typed here: `mid` is halfway in the reading from the place's own value to the bird's wall, `at` where it reaches a number of this row, `turns` where it first leaves its value at the bird's nought. A lean's `highFrom` is a cut of the same kinds where its high lean starts, in place of the band's upper third. A lean's `lowTo` is a cut of the same kinds where its low lean ends, in place of the band's lower third (Spark's still band: the still end is whole from the band's edge to where `still` turns, one program for most seeds, so the cell holds the low lean's line over all of it). `drums: false` holds only while the drums are off. `sub` and `lockedSays` are the locked reading, filled from the record (`{hand}`, `{handWord}`, `{caller}`, `{answerer}`); `without` names what a line, a lean or the block says where a fact of the program is false (`hand`: the hand the record names never strikes, as at Spark's still end). Tide keeps the general words (the sound close, open or wide is what it does here too). Read only where the theme's program carries the conversation: a library turn at BELLS reads the general words.",
