   "birds": {
    "says": "about the place's own birds: Tide the sea's size and distance (larger and farther, the sends up and the spray's top duller; smaller, nearer and drier down, and the bloom, nearer, a little louder: a calm sea is quieter in motion and never inaudible); Root the undertow's weight (the rumble louder and longer; the bass a little down, since Root's own seasoning makes the sub's body heavier, so the weight is the body's and not the level's); Veil the sea state (rougher up: the period shorter, the swell's band broader so the periods scatter more, the chop stronger, a cross swell more often; calmer down: a long clean groundswell); Zephyr the surf's brightness (the spray louder and its top more open); and what Tide and Veil take from the sea, measured (`measuredDb`: where the theme's trim windows measure at nought against the place's own, dB a unit of the bird, fitted on the paired windows of the 24 own themes at six pulls, the bloom's nearness in: Tide 2.1, Veil 2.3, each pull within 0.2 dB), so the trim follows them and a calm sea is quieter in motion, never inaudible",
