akSteps after the kick, back on the path fallSteps later, then sags at sagStPerStep to the run's next travel, at most sagMaxSt deep, lifted, never cut, over the register's floor less underFloorSt; its knobs are flickSt, sagStPerStep and sagMaxSt. knobs: the phrase's gestures as declared ranges, the written phrase at their defaults (a setting none yet writes; birds later): scoop scales every pitch knot's residual over its anchor path, afterKick's flick and sag with it, never the anchors (0: the anchors' plain path), swell every level knot's distance from 1 (0: flat), pairOnHold every pair share (0: no pair), edge every body knot's distance from 1 (0: no accent), pressDb the low duck a pressed kick asks. play: how the line is played — the lowest note (floor, MIDI; E1) and the most over the register's ceiling (ceilingOver, semitones); the accent on its steps (on) and elsewhere (off); the line stepping aside under each backbeat (dips: steps, dB, from earlyS seconds before); the release into the next run or the bar's end (touching) and into a rest (resting); a run that touches holds holdS seconds over, one that rests lets go at restShare of its length; a change takes at most changeShare of its gap; a phrase run ends phraseGapS before its length; outside the riff a note holds into the next where the gap is gapSteps or less (joined, of the onsets' distance) and else plays detached of its length, a slide in held slideOverS over the next onset. trimDb (on the phrase): the riff's level against V's in the same voice, in dB, on the gain of every note it plays.",
