  "provenance": {
    "source": "the catalog's source 8, a drum and bass mix (mining id 8)",
    "passage": "954.682-976.751 s of the source, 16 bars at 174 BPM; the phrase is its bars 1-8",
    "reading": "the bass line read with phase off the 22-120 Hz band of the mix: a dominant-peak and phase-slope pitch path, the main component demodulated along it (level and fine pitch), a pair partner tested in 0.6 s holds; the per-sixteenth map gives the shapes, the sounding spans the runs (notes/rounds/liquid-riffs.md)",
    "character": "a busy two-bar figure that climbs and steps down in glides, then a bar of rest every four bars",
    "adopted": "revision 2 (liquid-riffs-2, 10-08, notes/rounds/liquid-riffs-2.md): moved from the mined candidates into the liquid place's riff table, drawn by weight beside V's where the birds stand toward Spark and Loom, the busy and the phrase. The pitch knots re-encoded in the loader's format since liquid-fix (each knot's note as an anchor, its offset as the residual: the same straight path, the register now chosen once); the phrase's knobs V's; the pair share 1 throughout where it read 0, so the riff plays V's body (the unequal pair, and the voice's third harmonic following it); the play block V's whole, its pairClock with it, as the place's way of playing a line. V's own rules stay V's: no afterKick, no double slides, no body accents, no press",
    "grit": "its source reads a stronger second harmonic (-27.6 dBc against -40.7 in the held source and -41.1 in source 9); the voice declares no per-note second harmonic, so the riff plays V's body as it is, and its grit is open (a voice control, not row data)",
    "limits": "the phrase is the passage's bars 1-8 (the loader's eight bars), so the fourth-bar rest every four bars is kept once a phrase; two spans of 48 sixteenths are split at 32 and 96 (the loader's 32-sixteenth run), re-attacked legato there where the source holds through",
    "level": "phrase.trimDb -3.7 (liquid-riffs-2, 10-08): at pair share 1 the riff read +3.7 to +4.3 dB over V's line in the 25-160 Hz band (integrated loudness of the bass alone through the app's own offline render, a drop's sixteen bars on seeds 1, 4 and 5 of its corner, V on the same seed and theme; its notes sit higher over home than V's, which the loudness weighs more); trimmed, +0.4 to +1.0 in loudness and -0.9 to -1.2 in unweighted band level",
    "status": "adopted 10-08 on his approved plan for the liquid place's riffs; the weights and the trim are first guesses for his ear",
    "trimmed": "revision 3 (riff-trim, 10-10): bridges and play.growl taken out of the row; nothing has read them since the review of 10-08 (A4) took out the code that laid them (the mined bars' bridges, the growl over the line), so every program plays as before"
