  "provenance": {
    "module": "piano.ts",
    "round": "sounds-r3",
    "note": "The piano, synthesised and mostly heard as a room: six stretched partials per string and a second string a few cents flat, a band-passed hammer, two stages of decay with the upper partials going first, velocity setting the level and the brightness. It owns the settings' `piano` block (the composer's half — register, the sends' rolls, the arpeggio's chances — sits beside it there), so a room voices it: house-v2's present piano lifts the dry note, the sustain and slows the upper partials.",
    "notes": {
      "dryLevel": "The dry note is quiet; the hall is the instrument.",
      "partialDecay": "Per partial index: the top of the note goes first, which is the whole reason the note darkens.",
      "stretchCents": "String stiffness: a couple of cents on the second partial, growing quadratically up the stack.",
      "timbres": "The piano as it describes itself for the loudness fit: a struck string whose sustain is 0.26 of its attack and whose brightness runs from 1.5 to 5.4 kHz on velocity — the middle of that stands here. Its loudness is the fit's input and is left where the fit was blessed: the channel pin on the lowpass (the click repair of 09-22) made the piano play 0.7-1.0 dB louder on its fixture and 0.9 dB louder in the golden 1:0 window, and measured by the definition this number was taken on it would read about -16.0; writing it would move the trims of every v1 theme whose keys die rolled the piano, which is not moved for a repair. It moves with the next refit of the loudness model.",
      "measured": "The piano alone on its own fixture through the real graph, eight bars of its figure, integrated, less the level its table gave it: the scene every kitchen voice is held to (tools/test-voices.ts), in both engines at both rates, within a decibel. MEASURED and written by that gate's --bless. Before the channel pin the same scene read -21.2 in Chromium and -21.5 in Firefox; with it, -20.5 in both.",
      "controls": "Per-note controls let a sustained piano phrase and short chord stabs share the instrument without revoicing the theme; omission plays the room's numbers. `harmonicBody` 0 is no body; `ring` is how far past its written length the note rings."
    }
  }
