  "provenance": {
    "module": "keys.ts",
    "round": "sounds-r3",
    "note": "The electric piano, 35% of tracks and the commonest keyboard in the study: a sine carrier, a 1:1 modulator for the body and a 1:14 one for the tine whose index is gone in 120 ms, a fixed lowpass with a resonant lift at the measured 3.6 kHz formant, attack 24 ms, 8.7 dB down at 300 ms and still only 7.7 dB down at the bar line, and a 5.2 Hz tremolo that pans as well as swells. A style voices its tone (`keyboardPatches.ep`). The patch is its own (what was `KEYBOARD_PRESETS`); the amplifier it plays through is the room's `keys` block, which all five share. Its timbre's loudness is MEASURED (2026-09-17, tools/loudness-fit.ts --timbres): this family alone in an eight-bar main groove, metered, less the level its room gave it, median over the themes that rolled it; it belongs to the instrument and not the room. The other three facts are read off the patch and held to it: struck where it is not an organ, the hold its sustain, the brightness its corner.",
    "notes": {
      "attack": "The envelope is the measured level at 300 ms and at the bar line, turned into an envelope: attack, decay and the sustain fraction.",
      "hpHz": "The keys reach down into the band the kick body tops out in.",
      "tremoloHz": "MEASURED: 27% of tracks carry a 4-7 Hz tremolo; the electric piano family has the highest AM prominence of the sustained families.",
      "edge": "Round SPARK-1: the note's own oscillators high-passed at the place's corner and summed in after the lowpass, falling from the strike to a fraction of itself, and a few milliseconds of band-passed noise on the onset; a place writes it (the house's row). At rest its level and its strike are nought, which builds nothing, over the corners the house writes.",
      "knobs": "The keyboard's ranges (PLAN-MODULATION M1): five patches behind one name, so each default is the median of the five — 1900/2600/1800/2500/2000 Hz of corner, 0.30/0.32/0.37/0.72/0.048 of sustain, 30/22/24/9/11 ms of attack — and what a knob moves is a factor on whichever patch is playing; a setting in absolute hertz would make one instrument out of five. The ceiling on brightness is the one the voice has always had: the note's own lowpass is clamped at 9 kHz. The grain (round SPARK-1) is a factor on the edge and the strike a place writes, one at the house; its measured slope is the keys alone under the house's edge against none, seed 1 theme two, +0.002 LU."
    }
  }
