    "lowLean": 3,
    "says": "Full passages sit in the manual's 60-72, the lower dyads leaned toward (lowLean: a dyad a semitone lower weighs that much more per twelve semitones), over the bass's room; a lifted (exposed) passage, where the bass rests, takes the low-mid 50-66 band that reads as breath and not as ringing (his wavePad reference, 10-11).",
