    "thinVel": 0.85,
    "oneToneVel": 0.7,
    "swell": {
      "db": -14,
      "oct": 2.5
    },
    "says": "Darker than a struck or breathed detail: the voice's own corner at cutoffMul. Every note opens over its own crest (an entrance swell: from db under and oct octaves darker to its level and tone over the note's attack), so the tone rises with the breath and does not sweep open in half a second and sit. `levelDb`: the bed's crest brought back to where round 1's stood (measured on rendered stems: the darker, lower, two-note bed read 4.4 dB under in A's first passage and 7.3 dB under in B's exposed passage), so this round changes the bed's phrasing and not its place in the mix.",
