    "reading": "the hats thinned or the top down on 2.2 bars in 16 of the reference mains (1.25 + 0.99); on the bar before a sixteen-bar line as often as on any other (0.0-0.25 against 0.07-0.18 over the four cuts), so the line is the house's idiom and the draw's, not the reading's",
