  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "trance: four on the floor with the bass on every offbeat eighth between the kicks, open hats on the same offbeats, a clap on two and four",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar: the kick on the beats and the bass answering it on each and \u2014 the bounce every trance record from the late nineties rides \u2014 the root for three and the fifth under it for the last. A path cannot open on a rest, so each bar starts with a ghost of the root under the kick, a tenth of the weight and a tenth of a beat long. Open hats double the bass offbeats, closed sixteenths are left out. 136-140 is above the fast band's top (130), so it plays at 130 under the Techno key: trance has no key of its own yet.",
