  "provenance": {
    "round": "sounds-r2",
    "module": "formant-pad.ts",
    "note": "A formant pad: a breathy, vocal-ish sustained voice. Two saws and a little noise through three parallel bandpasses parked where a vowel's formants are, and the vowel drifts from one to another and back over about twenty seconds. It is the sustained role for music that is not made of chords on a keyboard, and it holds as well as it plays a note.",
    "notes": {
      "vowels": "Two vowels and the slow walk between them. The three numbers are the formant centres in Hz; the pad sits between `vowel` and `vowelTo` and wanders across at `driftHz`.",
      "q": "The three bandpasses: how sharp each is and how loud. The first formant carries the body and the third is the breath on top of it.",
      "detuneCents": "What goes into them: two saws a few cents apart, and the breath."
    }
  }
