  "provenance": {
    "round": "bells-birds",
    "module": "mallets.ts",
    "note": "Small bells, as crotales and hand bells are (bells-birds, his ask of 10-18: 'if i want more lighter bells composition i would thin root'): a small bell is high and rings short, so its fundamental rings 5 s where the temple bell's prime rings 12. The fundamental and its pair a hair apart, the octave (2), and two short upper partials (2.92, 4.16) that are the sparkle of a small cast bell. A brass striker: a band at 5 kHz for 2 ms.",
    "notes": {
      "beating": "The fundamental's pair at 1.0025 shimmers 1.6-3.9 Hz over the small bells' register (MIDI 76-91): a small bell's quick tremble, where a great bell's beat is slow.",
      "partials": "Five, all short: a strike holds its oscillators five seconds at most, so a call of small bells costs the ceiling little.",
      "edge": "Not read by the harmonic bus's edge, as vibes."
    }
  }
